{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1792044012,"nonce":"IePi63NqbcocFKqgGTVX4lD2tX0=","target":"99a449019a5076bac36e80287b49f1296740a5c125f3d855532c1a0d67059509","message":"Three visual changes, decided by the user:\n\n1. A group header carries its own divider, on every view kind (list, board, gantt, matrix): the label (bold, in the group colour as before), a space, then a faint rule of `─` to the window's edge. One helper, `groupHeader` in tui/render.go, draws it for all four; a nested list group's rule runs from after its indented label; the gantt's crosshair still runs through the header, rule included.\n2. An issue's own title is bold wherever a view draws it: the list's title cell (bold under the wash and inside the reversed cursor cell), the board card's title lines, the gantt's label when the label is the title. Keyed on schema.TitleKey. Show already bolds the title.\n3. Links: linked id faint and underlined, linked title plain, shared across all views including show. One helper, `linkStyled` in tui/link.go, draws every relation value (`\u003cid\u003e \u003ctitle\u003e`, comma-separated) on list, board, gantt (a relation label), matrix (a relation row axis), show and new: the id is faint and underlined, the only underline on a page and the cue that enter follows it; the title and the commas are plain, so a linked title never outweighs the row's own bold title. Under the reversed cursor cell nothing is faint, the id keeps its underline. An id that does not resolve is the id piece alone. The plain text is unchanged; truncation cuts by display width with the styles kept. styleLink is gone.","files":null}]}